  5: { id: 'qc-5', type: 'multiple-choice', title: 'Safe Months', instructions: 'Read the question. Choose the answer from Chapter 5.', question: 'Why could more people visit Mecca to perform Hajj?', options: ['Mecca was far from the busy trade routes, so the roads were quiet.', 'In the sacred months people stayed away from fighting, so the region was safer.', 'The Quraysh leaders stopped all trade during the pilgrimage season.'], correctAnswer: 1, explanation: 'Chapter 5 says the sacred months “made the region safer. In these months, people focused on worship, showed respect, and stayed away from fighting. Because of this safe atmosphere, more people could visit the city to perform Hajj.”', feedback: { correct: 'Right. The sacred months made the region safe, and this safe atmosphere brought more pilgrims.', incorrect: 'Read the last paragraph of Chapter 5 and find the words “Because of this …”. What made the region safer?' } },
  6: { id: 'qc-6', type: 'multiple-choice', title: 'Pilgrims and Business', instructions: 'Read the question. Choose the answer from Chapter 6.', question: 'Why did business grow quickly in Mecca during the pilgrimage season?', options: ['Many people came for religious practices, and big trade fairs took place at the same time.', 'Lending money with usury was not allowed during the pilgrimage season.', 'People went to Arafat first, so the fairs were empty and prices were low.'], correctAnswer: 0, explanation: 'Chapter 6 says the pilgrimage practices “kept Mecca active during the pilgrimage season. This religious activity also helped business grow quickly. Big trade fairs such as Ukaz, Majannah, and Dhul-Majaz took place during this time.” People attended the fairs first and then went to Arafat.', feedback: { correct: 'Correct. Religious activity and the big fairs came together, so business grew quickly.', incorrect: 'Read the first two paragraphs of Chapter 6. What kept Mecca active, and what took place “during this time”?' } },
  7: { id: 'qc-7', type: 'matching', matchingHeadings: { left: 'In Chapter 7', right: 'What the chapter says about it' }, title: 'The Gap Between Rich and Poor', instructions: 'Match each idea with what Chapter 7 says about it.', question: 'How does Chapter 7 describe life for the rich and the poor?', matchingPairs: [{ left: 'High interest', right: 'Many people could not pay back what they owed.' }, { left: 'Money and tribe', right: 'They were the most important values for the wealthy Quraysh.' }, { left: 'Orphans and weak people', right: 'Their property was often taken by force.' }], correctAnswer: { 'High interest': 'Many people could not pay back what they owed.', 'Money and tribe': 'They were the most important values for the wealthy Quraysh.', 'Orphans and weak people': 'Their property was often taken by force.' }, explanation: 'Chapter 7 says many people “could not pay back their debts because of high interest”, that “for the wealthy Quraysh, money and tribe were the most important values”, and that orphans and weak people were treated badly while “powerful people often took their property by force.”', feedback: { correct: 'Well done. Each link shows how the gap between rich and poor hurt people who had no power.', incorrect: 'The first paragraph explains debt, the second gives the values of the wealthy Quraysh, and the last sentence is about orphans and weak people.' } },
