  10: { id: 'qc-10', type: 'multiple-choice', title: 'Allah and the Idols', instructions: 'Read the question. Choose the answer from Chapter 10.', question: 'Many Arabs believed in Allah as the Creator. Why did they also worship idols?', options: ['They thought the idols had created the world.', 'They wanted to check omens before making decisions.', 'They thought the idols helped them talk to Allah.'], correctAnswer: 2, explanation: 'Chapter 10 says Arab people “actually believed in one main God, Allah, as the Creator. However, they also worshipped many idols. They thought these idols helped them talk to Allah.” Omens are mentioned too, but as a superstition, not as the reason for the idols.', feedback: { correct: 'Correct. They saw the idols as a way to reach Allah, even though they believed Allah was the Creator.', incorrect: 'Read the second paragraph of Chapter 10. Find the sentence after “However, they also worshipped many idols.”' } },
